    /**
     * THE SAME STOP, WHEN THE THING THAT CAUSED IT IS ABLOH (captain's ruling, 2026-08-31).
     *
     * WHY A SECOND CODE RATHER THAN A CONDITIONAL OWNER. `owner` is declared per code and read as a
     * literal by the parity tests that hold this registry honest, so a code whose owner depended on
     * its facts would be a mechanism nobody could check. Two causes with two owners and two remedies
     * are two codes, which is what the registry is for.
     *
     * WHEN IT IS RAISED. `swagger-api/swagger-ui` read `preflight-refused, owned by environment` over
     * a `dist/` that its own `Build SwaggerUI` step had written, on both cycles of the fresh-ten run.
     * Nothing about their environment was wrong: abloh's step was standing at the END of their job,
     * behind every step that writes into the tree, and that placement is abloh's. The step now goes
     * immediately behind the step that runs their suite, so this code is for the case where it did
     * not - and `preflight.ts` marks the finding rather than this code guessing.
     *
     * THE REMEDY IS THE EDIT THAT MOVES THE STEP, and the run's own message names the block and the
     * line. `docs/lessons/a-remedy-is-a-promise.md`: the state this refusal names is cleared by
     * moving abloh's step, and by nothing the maintainer could do to their environment.
     */
